      </ul>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the front matter</strong> <code>&lt;frontmatter&gt;</code> holds everything before chapter 1. Two things are in it that you might expect at the top of the map:
      <ul>
      <li>The maprefs to the subject scheme and the two key definition maps, the <code>common-notes</code> and <code>start-here</code> keydefs, and the resource-only reference to <code>common-steps</code>. A bookmap's content model is strict: at the top level it allows only <code>&lt;booktitle&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;bookmeta&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;frontmatter&gt;</code>, chapters, parts, appendixes, <code>&lt;backmatter&gt;</code> and reltables, in that order. Key definitions and resource-only references go inside <code>&lt;frontmatter&gt;</code>, and the demo at the end shows what happens when they do not.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;booklists&gt;</code> names the generated lists: <code>&lt;toc/&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;figurelist/&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;tablelist/&gt;</code> are empty elements, and the PDF transform fills them from the book. <code>&lt;notices&gt;</code> points at the license topic from stage 18, and <code>&lt;preface&gt;</code> at <em>What is Audacity?</em>. Both are topicrefs with a role.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the body and the back matter</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;part navtitle="…"&gt;</code> groups chapters and prints as <em>Part I</em>, <em>Part II</em>; each <code>&lt;chapter href&gt;</code> is a topic and its nested <code>&lt;topicref&gt;</code>s are its sections. The keys the topicrefs carried in the full guide, <code>digital-audio</code>, <code>install</code>, <code>podcast-workflow</code>, <code>formats</code> and <code>effects</code>, are carried here too, so the <code>&lt;xref keyref&gt;</code>s and the license topic's <code>&lt;xref keyref="start-here"/&gt;</code> resolve in the book.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;appendix href&gt;</code> after the parts: the three reference topics become <em>Appendix A</em>, <em>Appendix B</em> and <em>Appendix C</em>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;backmatter&gt;</code> holds a second <code>&lt;booklists&gt;</code>: a <code>&lt;glossarylist&gt;</code> with the seven glossary topics inside it, so they print as one glossary, and an empty <code>&lt;indexlist/&gt;</code>, which asks the transform for an index built from the <code>&lt;indexterm&gt;</code> elements in the prolog metadata of stage 13. The index is the last entry in the contents list in step 3.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-2-the-deliverable" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 2: The deliverable<a href="#step-2-the-deliverable" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Add the deliverable</strong> Choose <strong>Project</strong> &gt; <strong>Project Tools</strong> &gt; <strong>Manage Deliverables...</strong> and click <strong>Add...</strong>. Enter these values:
      <Table class="my-4">
      <TableHeader>
      <TableRow>
      <TableHead>Field</TableHead>
      <TableHead>Value</TableHead>
      </TableRow>
      </TableHeader>
      <TableBody>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><strong>Name</strong></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>book-pdf</code></TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><strong>Input map</strong></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>audacity-book.ditamap</code></TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><strong>DITAVAL (optional)</strong></TableCell>
      <TableCell>(leave empty)</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><strong>Transtype</strong></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>pdf</code></TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><strong>Output (optional)</strong></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>out/book-pdf</code></TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><strong>Publication parameters</strong></TableCell>
      <TableCell>(none)</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      </TableBody>
      </Table>
      <p>Change <strong>Transtype</strong> from <code>html5</code> to <code>pdf</code>. Click <strong>Save...</strong>, click <strong>OK</strong> to write the deliverable, and click <strong>Close</strong>.</p>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read it</strong> The eighth deliverable, <code>book-pdf</code>, is the bookmap with the <code>pdf</code> transtype. DITA-OT's built-in PDF transform, <code>org.dita.pdf2</code>, renders the book with Apache FOP. The editor includes both, and <strong>Check Project</strong> builds the PDF with the other seven deliverables into <code>out/book-pdf/</code>.
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-3-update-the-readme-and-check-your-work" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 3: Update the README and check your work<a href="#step-3-update-the-readme-and-check-your-work" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Change the "You are on" line and the layout</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n Build a guide through 27 stages. Maps begin at stage 02; HTML publication begins at stage 03.\n \n-You are on stage 18: chunking and output.\n+You are on stage 19: bookmap.\n \n ## Stages\n "} lang="diff" title="README.md" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Format and check your work</strong>
      <p>Format the files:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml format -i topics/*.dita *.ditamap"} lang="bash" />
      <p>Then check the project. In the editor, choose <strong>Project</strong> &gt; <strong>Check Project</strong> and read the result in the <strong>Project Validation</strong> panel. From the command line, run:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml check ."} lang="bash" />
      <p>Example output:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"health   clean\nbuild    full                 ok  /home/you/audacity-guide/out/full\nbuild    beginner-mac         ok  /home/you/audacity-guide/out/beginner-mac\nbuild    beginner-windows     ok  /home/you/audacity-guide/out/beginner-windows\nbuild    podcaster-linux      ok  /home/you/audacity-guide/out/podcaster-linux\nbuild    review               ok  /home/you/audacity-guide/out/review\nbuild    install-variants     ok  /home/you/audacity-guide/out/install-variants\nbuild    collection           ok  /home/you/audacity-guide/out/collection\nbuild    book-pdf             ok  /home/you/audacity-guide/out/book-pdf\n  PDF rendering reported 4 warnings (1 The contents of fo:external-graphic line n exceed the available area in the inline-progres…, 1 The contents of fo:instream-foreign-object line n exceed the available area in the inline-…, 1 The contents of fo:inline line n exceed the available area in the inline-progression direc…, and 1 other kind)\noutput   wrote a file, no pages to check links in book-pdf\noutput   clean (full, beginner-mac, beginner-windows, podcaster-linux, review, install-variants, collection)\nReady: the project is healthy, every deliverable built, and the output of full, beginner-mac, beginner-windows, podcaster-linux, review, install-variants, collection holds together."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The check builds eight deliverables. The <code>book-pdf</code> line reports the PDF, and the indented line under it summarizes the layout warnings from Apache FOP, such as content that is wider than its column. The warnings do not fail the check. The output check reads links in HTML pages only, so for the PDF it confirms that the build wrote a file.</p>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the book</strong> The editor writes the PDF to <code>out/book-pdf/audacity-book.pdf</code> in your project. Open it in any PDF viewer. <code>pdftotext</code> shows the contents page without a viewer:
      <CodeBlock code={"pdftotext out/book-pdf/audacity-book.pdf - | sed -n '/^Contents/,/^Index/p'"} lang="bash" />
      <CodeBlock code={"Contents\nList of Figures..................................................................................................................................v\nList of Tables................................................................................................................................. vii\n\nAbout this guide.......................................................................................................ix\nPreface: What is Audacity?.................................................................................... xi\nPart I: Getting started............................................................................................ 13\nChapter 1: What is digital audio?................................................................ 15\nChapter 2: Installing Audacity......................................................................19\nPart II: Recording and editing.............................................................................. 21\nChapter 3: Preparing to record.................................................................... 23\nRecording your first track...................................................................................................................... 24\n\nChapter 4: Trimming audio...........................................................................25\nChapter 5: Removing background noise......................................................27\nWhy the order of effects matters........................................................................................................... 28\n\nChapter 6: Exporting audio...........................................................................29\nPart III: Podcasting.................................................................................................31\nChapter 7: Podcast production workflow.................................................... 33\nAppendix A: Supported audio formats.................................................................35\nAppendix B: Effects reference............................................................................... 37\n\nAppendix C: Presets................................................................................................39\nGlossary.......................................................................................................................................... 41\nIndex................................................................................................................................................43"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The PDF transform generates the numbered parts, chapters, and appendixes, the lists of figures and tables, the glossary, and the index from the bookmap. The license topic appears as the notices page.</p>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <p>Test the placement of key definitions. Move the two <code>&lt;keydef&gt;</code> lines out of <code>&lt;frontmatter&gt;</code> to directly after <code>&lt;/bookmeta&gt;</code>, and check your work. The check stops at health. Example output:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"health   NOT CLEAN\n  invalid: /home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-book.ditamap\n    86:11  The content of element type \"bookmap\" does not match its content model.\n  (run project-health for the full report)\nNot ready: the project itself has faults. The build and the built output were not checked."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p><code>&lt;bookmap&gt;</code> does not allow a <code>&lt;keydef&gt;</code> at its top level. The error is reported at the closing <code>&lt;/bookmap&gt;</code> tag, line 86, because that is where the parser stops matching the content model. The model is a title, then <code>&lt;bookmeta&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;frontmatter&gt;</code>, chapters or parts, appendixes, <code>&lt;backmatter&gt;</code>, and relationship tables, in that order. Because health failed, nothing was built. Keys, scheme maprefs and resource-only references live inside <code>&lt;frontmatter&gt;</code> in a bookmap.</p>
      <p>Undo the change and check again. Confirm that the check reports <code>Ready</code> before you continue.</p>
      <h2 id="what-you-learned" class="group scroll-mt-20">What you learned<a href="#what-you-learned" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;bookmap&gt;</code> and its DOCTYPE; <code>&lt;booktitle&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;mainbooktitle&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;booktitlealt&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;bookmeta&gt;</code>: <code>&lt;publisherinformation&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;bookid&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;bookpartno&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;edition&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;bookrights&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;copyrfirst&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;bookowner&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;frontmatter&gt;</code> holds the keydefs, maprefs and resource-only refs, the <code>&lt;booklists&gt;</code> (<code>&lt;toc&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;figurelist&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;tablelist&gt;</code>), <code>&lt;notices&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;preface&gt;</code>; <code>&lt;backmatter&gt;</code> holds <code>&lt;glossarylist&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;indexlist&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;part&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;chapter&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;appendix&gt;</code>, and how the PDF numbers them.</li>
      <li>A deliverable with the <code>pdf</code> transtype, added in <strong>Manage Deliverables</strong>.</li>
      <li>The bookmap content model defines the permitted metadata, book divisions, and relationship tables at the top level.</li>
      </ul>
